## PART B — NEXT-COEFF: **PARTIAL**

**YES.** The `n−m−1` identities `M_r = Tr(f τ^r / g_y) = [y^{n−1}](y^r f mod (g−c))` are remainder coefficients over `Q`. They vanish (resp. equal 1 at the monic index) on every charged control, including D15’s nine identities. No Puiseux, no semigroup, no outer/inner split.

**NO.** The coefficient of `x^{(k+1)c_max−1−j}` is not a function of tower data down to level `j` only.

First mixing coefficient: **B6, `k=8`, `R_8 = −2c`**. Invisible to the bottom star and to `chi_N = T^6+x`; it is the `T^3` term of the level-2 composition. Next: **B6, `k=10`, `R_10 = −1`**, which is not even in `(T^3−c)²+x` and needs the `−T` from `g = y+u³`. C6, D15 (`R_17=5c`, `R_20=15c²`), and a 3-fold square repeat the same slack-then-mix pattern.

Re-base the DEG block of `globalinterp.py` onto remainders in `Q[x,c][y]/(g−c)` (and onto `[T^{n−1}](T^k mod chi)` when `chi` is known). Do not filter `chi` by deficit, and do not claim a `g`-alone resultant: `Res_y(g−c, T−f)` still needs `f`.
